---
layout: layouts/runner.njk
title: Timed facts
description: A one-minute check of the First Grade addition and subtraction facts released so far. The parent marks each answer; the next fact comes up at once.
permalink: /timed/
exitUrl: /practice/
---
<div class="runner-start" id="timed-start" hidden>
  <article class="finish">
    <p class="finish__kicker">Timed facts</p>
    <h1 class="finish__title">One minute of facts</h1>
    <p class="finish__lead">The screen shows one fact at a time, drawn from the First Grade facts released so far. Say the fact. The child answers. Tap Firm or Error, and the next fact comes up at once. After one minute the screen shows how many were right, against a goal that rises as more facts are released.</p>
    <p class="finish__lead">A fact is automatic when the child answers it in under three seconds three times running. The fact chart on Records shows which are automatic, which are firm, and which are not yet.</p>
    <p class="finish__lead" id="timed-who"></p>
    <div class="btn-row btn-row--stack">
      <button type="button" class="btn btn--primary btn--block btn--big" data-start-timed>Start the minute</button>
    </div>
    <ul class="finish__links"><li><a href="/practice/">All practice</a></li><li><a href="/records/">Records</a></li></ul>
  </article>
</div>
{% set first = program.summary | selectattr("id", "equalto", "first") | first %}
<script id="runner-data" type="application/json">{"mode":"timed","exitUrl":"/practice/","seconds":60,"level":{"id":"first","name":"First Grade","lessons":{{ first.lessons }}},"facts":{{ program.facts.first | dump | safe }}}</script>
<script>
document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", function () {
  var who = document.getElementById("timed-who");
  if (who && window.mathProgress && window.mathProgress.getActiveProfile()) who.textContent = "Child: " + window.mathProgress.getActiveProfile().name + ".";
});
</script>
